"order":3,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"🎛️ NOVA AUDIO MASTERING PROCESS","properties":{"ue_properties":{"widget_ue_connectable":{},"version":"7.8","input_ue_unconnectable":{}}},"widgets_values":["\nMasters a file, stamps it with a catalogue identity, archives the report and\nthe audio under one name, and renders the report. Read the canvas left to\nright.\n\n\n📥 1. LOAD\n----------\n\nNova Load Audio. start_seconds 0 and duration_seconds 0 mean the whole file.\nchannel_mode native keeps the source layout. The file name is a working name\nonly - nothing downstream trusts it.\n\n\n🔄 2. FORCE A RE-RUN\n--------------------\n\nComfyUI skips a node whose inputs have not changed. The INT node wired to\nrun_count increments every run, so the master is actually recomputed. Leave it\non increment while tuning. The number is kept in the report as\nprovenance.run_count.\n\n\n🎚️ 3. MASTER\n------------\n\nNova Audio Master. mode Auto with profile Balanced does the deciding; the tonal\ntrims are all 0.00, so Auto is choosing them.\n\nmode Off bypasses mastering and fingerprints the file as it is. Useful for\nregistering an original you did not master, but that report is marked\nOBSERVATION_ONLY - it can show a file is unaltered, never that it matches a\nmaster.\n\n\n🗄️ 4. THE DATABASE FILLS THE IDENTITY NODE\n------------------------------------------\n\nNova SQLite Reader, column_set identity, with a where clause that selects ONE\ntrack. Its identity_json goes to Nova Master Identity's identity_fields_json\ninput. Every field it carries replaces the widget of the same name, so nothing\nis retyped after a browser reset. The console prints which fields came from the\ndatabase.\n\n* No database yet? Copy examples/nova_album_example.db out of the pack, point\n  database_path at your copy, and edit it in DB Browser for SQLite.\n* database_path is an absolute path and will not exist on another machine. Set\n  it, and table_name, before the first run.\n\n\n☝️ ONE ROW ONLY\n---------------\n\nThe identity preset refuses a query that matches several tracks, and lists what\nit found. Narrow the where clause:\n\nTitle = 'Nine Hours North'\n\n\n🔤 EXACT NAMES WIN\n------------------\n\nA table may carry both Copyright and copyright_owner, or Comment and notes. The\ncolumn named exactly like an Identity field is used. Tag columns only fill what\nis left empty.\n\n\n⚠️ VERSION IS NOT DECORATION\n----------------------------\n\narchive_name is built from track number, initials, title, version and delivery\nformat. Two masters of one track sharing a version produce the same file name,\nand the second OVERWRITES the first with no warning. Give them different version\nstrings - Album Version, Source, Radio Edit - and both survive, and\nidentity_selector can pick either.\n\n\nℹ️ DELIVERY INTENT ONLY\n-----------------------\n\ntarget_bit_depth and target_sample_rate describe what the release is meant to\nbe. Nothing is converted here. The save node decides the real encoding.\n\n\n🔍 5. WHAT THE VALIDATOR IS DOING HERE\n--------------------------------------\n\nWith reference_report_json connected it is not checking anything - it is writing\nthe archive. Feed it identity_json, not report_json: only the Identity output\ncarries the catalogue block, and whatever arrives here is exactly what is\nstored. save_reference_json must be true.\n\n\n🗂️ ONE NAME, TWO FOLDERS\n------------------------\n\nThe report is filed in report_path under the archive name. archive_audio_path\ndrives the Save Audio node's file_path, with filename_mode set to exact\n(overwrite), so the audio lands beside it under the same name.\n\n\n⚠️ THE BIT_EXACT HERE IS FREE\n-----------------------------\n\nThis node runs before the save, on the tensor, so it compares the master against\nits own report and always agrees. It proves the archive was written, not that\nthe delivered file is good.\n\n\n🔬 OPTIONAL - CHECK THE FILE THAT SHIPS\n---------------------------------------\n\nAdd a second validator after the save, fed by the Save Audio node's audio output\nwith reload_after_save ON, archive_name wired from Identity, and\nsave_reference_json OFF. That one reads the file back off disk and compares it\nto the archive just written. Expect REPRODUCTION_MATCH, not BIT_EXACT -\nquantising to 16 or 24 bit changes the samples, and matching within tolerance is\nthe correct pass. It is the only place in the graph where the delivered file is\nmeasured.\n\n\n📊 6. THE REPORT\n----------------\n\nNova Master Report Viewer renders report_json. view_mode, theme and font_scale\nrestyle an already rendered report without re-running the graph. Right-click to\nexport every view as images.\n\nCONDITIONAL_PASS is not a failure. It means release-safe with a reference target\nnot fully reached, because reaching it would have cost more than it was worth."],"color":"#432","bgcolor":"#653"},{"id":15,"type":"NovaPlayerNode","pos":[-268.2458438440991,-11606.963543171572],"size":[941.6161171574838,867.8853233034497],"flags":{},"order":9,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"audio","name":"audio","type":"AUDIO","link":85},{"localized_name":"panel_format","name":"panel_format","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"panel_format"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"context","name":"context","shape":7,"type":"STRING","widget":{"name":"context"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"panel_info","name":"panel_info","type":"STRING","links":null}],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"NovaPlayerNode","ue_properties":{"widget_ue_connectable":{},"input_ue_unconnectable":{},"version":"7.8"},"lastAudioData":{"filename":"nova_player_ca71376c.wav","audio_sha256":"1150c7ba975a90696badbd559998fdd603c0810edd55c3128458a8ec8f46c538","context":null,"duration":234.374,"sample_rate":48000,"stereo":true,"lufs":-12.3,"bench":{"peak_db":-1.01,"peak_linear":0.889832,"rms_db":-14.81,"rms_mono_db":-15.46,"crest_db":13.8,"dc_offset":-0.000004,"over_fs":0,"clipped_samples":0,"clipped_pct":0,"lr_corr":0.722,"bands":{"BASS":54.99,"MID":35.09,"PRES":7.72,"HF":2.2},"hf_outliers":0,"samples":11249928,"channels":2},"filesize":44999756}},"widgets_values":["json","",{"viewMode":"combined_suite","volume":1,"muted":false,"looping":false,"theme":"nova-dark","panelOpen":false,"panelWidth":248,"openSection":"settings","colorScope":"node","overrides":{"roles":{},"renderers":{}}}]}],"links":[[82,25,0,24,0,"AUDIO"],[85,26,0,15,0,"AUDIO"],[87,24,3,27,0,"STRING"],[90,28,4,27,28,"STRING"],[92,24,0,30,0,"AUDIO"],[93,27,0,30,1,"STRING"],[94,27,2,30,5,"STRING"],[95,30,0,26,0,"AUDIO"],[98,30,5,26,1,"STRING"],[101,24,3,32,0,"STRING"],[102,35,0,24,1,"INT"]],"groups":[{"id":1,"title":"Nova Audio Mastering Process","bounding":[-2133.3857666406216,-12121.02622503018,3839.2633590936375,1399.1276422273295],"color":"#444","flags":{}}],"config":{},"extra":{"ds":{"scale":0.6454545454545578,"offset":[2233.339199441929,12388.216182086122]},"ue_links":[],"links_added_by_ue":[]},"version":0.4}